From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GNOME Window Appearance <gnome-window-appearance@chillet.moe>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: Add native shadows to Wayland windows

Paint one compositor-owned shadow beneath eligible Wayland surface trees,
using the same rounded frame geometry as the native alpha clip. Reuse
Mutter's cached nine-slice shadow implementation and keep focused and
unfocused variants, while clipping the shadow away from the transparent
window corners.

Include shadow bounds in the window actor paint volume. Because the shadow
is painted by the window actor before its children, Shell animations and
clones transform the content and shadow together without an extra window
texture pass.

Build the existing generic shadow factory and shape helpers independently
of Xwayland so Wayland-only builds retain the feature.

Target: Mutter 50.4
Depends-on: 0002-compositor-round-wayland-surface-trees.patch
Tested-by: scripts/test-mutter-patches.sh
Tested-by: tests/run-mutter-nested.sh
---

